From ef42f3bdc78c191bcaeb398538d39641f0c5ae2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotsunchip <hotsunchip@kaist.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 15:30:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Exit hyperlink formatting on Enter and Space

Inserting or pasting a link left the caret flush against its href
run, and applyInsertText/applySplitBlock blindly inherit the style
of whatever run touches the caret. So the very next Enter or Space
silently pulled new text into the same hyperlink instead of starting
plain text, forcing users to manually strip formatting afterward.

Reuse the existing pending-style controller: when the caret sits at
a link's trailing edge, arm pending with href: undefined (merged
onto the caret's current style so bold/italic etc. survive) so the
next typed character - first char of a new paragraph on Enter, or a
typed space - exits the link instead of extending it.
