Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Correct Slides applicability claim in the todo, doc no-op
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CodeRabbit review on PR #520 caught that the todo file claimed this
fix "applies to Slides too" because text-box-editor.ts wraps the
same TextEditor class. False: that host never calls setPendingStyle,
so pending stays null there and exitLinkIfAtTrailingEdge's
pending?.set(...) is a silent no-op — Enter/Space/paste can still
extend a link in a Slides text box.

Wiring pending into Slides is left as a follow-up rather than bolted
on here: it would either quietly enable the whole pending-style
toolbar-toggle feature for Slides with no dedicated test of that
surface, or need a parallel non-pending reimplementation — both
larger than this Docs-scoped bug fix warrants.
